QueryC is a search engine for standard libraries.
currently it includes all the functions in stdio.h and
string.h (72 so far). in due course Rust and C++ will
also be supported.

whilst I have unfortunately vibecoded the entire thing,
the UI was designed to be both simple and user friendly.
if shit works it works.

each signature and standard links directly to the line in
either a WG14 draft standard or an MSVC header file where
it is defined. bun run validate then re-scans these 338
lines.


Running it
----------

  bun install     install dependencies
  bun run dev     dev server at http://localhost:5173
  bun run build   static site in dist/

you need Bun. to check data and compile the examples, you
also need clang with the Windows SDK and MSVC Build Tools
headers.


Checking it
-----------

  bun run lint       ESLint, Stylelint, Prettier
  bun run validate   check data against its sources


Searching
---------

very self explanatory no? you type in box and it shows
you. it also shows not recommended functions if they are
fucky enough.


Contributing
------------

If you want to make any contributions, just contact me,
or just directly do a pr.

